    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "The System Nobody Wants To Touch",
      "script": "While that technical story was unfolding, a quieter, more commercial one landed at the same time. On April 4th, Anthropic cut off third-party agent harnesses \u2014 tools like OpenClaw and Hermes that had been authenticating through the same OAuth tokens as Claude Code \u2014 from running on subscription billing. Overnight, those wrappers needed separate, metered, pay-as-you-go usage to keep working. Claude Code and Claude Cowork, Anthropic's own sanctioned surfaces, stayed fully covered. Everything built outside that boundary got a bill. If you've maintained enterprise systems, you know this move. It's the platform owner deciding which integrations are partners and which ones are just unpriced load on their infrastructure. I've been on both sides of that line.",
      "words": 116,
      "card_script": "April 4th: sanctioned tools stayed covered. Everything outside that boundary got metered.",
