    {
      "id": 6,
      "name": "What This Means For The Industry",
      "script": "Zoom out and there's a real tension here that Anthropic itself is naming: maximum model performance wants maximum autonomy \u2014 a model with a shell and a REPL and minimal restriction. But enterprises can't ship that without controls, because autonomy without accountability is a compliance nightmare. The proposed answer isn't going back to rigid harnesses. It's a different kind of infrastructure: sandboxed execution environments, persistent and queryable memory, immutable audit trails for every action the agent took. That's a meaningful shift for the ecosystem of startups that built businesses around being the harness. Some of that category gets compressed into the model itself. What survives is the layer enterprises will always need: proof of what happened, and a boundary around what's allowed to happen.",
      "words": 124,
      "card_script": "The model wants autonomy. The enterprise wants proof and boundaries. That gap is the next product category.",
