    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "What I'm Exploring Next",
      "script": "So here's what I'm actually doing with this, not just thinking about it. I'm going back through tooling I've built around agents this year and asking, scene by scene, which piece exists because the model needed it, and which piece exists because I assumed it would. Some of it stays \u2014 anything that's really an audit boundary, a permission check, a place where I need a record of what the agent decided and why. That's not scaffolding, that's governance, and it doesn't go away. But the prompt-chaining-for-the-sake-of-control stuff, the hand-built filters doing a job a sandboxed shell can now do itself \u2014 I'm cutting that, deliberately, and measuring what breaks. I'll be sharing what I find, because I suspect most of us built more harness than we needed.",
      "words": 128,
      "card_script": "What stays: audit and permissions. What goes: control for control's sake. I'm testing that line live.",
